(runCFins): a callback from one is GHC\\'s error"] [123 21 "// +RTS -xq: the allocation limit's grace, bytes (0: GHC's 100k)"] [124 2 "// the threaded way (threaded.go, HES84 (a)): the program linked -threaded; enabled_capabilities, +RTS -N's count and"] [125 2 "// the label's address; the safe foreign calls in flight and their returns; the spark pool"] [134 2 "// the program's own C threads (queue 430): the ids of the threads its C started (cprog.go's clone), the timespec of"] [135 2 "// cIdle's nap, and each C thread's capability its in-calls are locked to (rts_setInCallCapability)"] [146 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [149 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [156 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [197 2 "// in place (HES73): the popped slot's fields written, no frame copied (its x and n are zero: pop clears them)"] [203 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [206 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [215 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [233 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update; a transaction aborts first and reruns from its start"] [234 3 "// after the wake-up (review 189, F2, the user's decision: the other threads never see its writes)"] [252 4 "// two update frames in a row (the lower thunk's evaluation is entering this one): squeezed as GHC's"] [253 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [254 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [255 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [261 5 "// in place, as pushCase"] [271 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [280 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [284 30 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [295 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [335 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [345 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [348 2 "// the two frequent frames read in place (HES73): no frame copied out, its pointers cleared"] [382 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value lost as GHC's"] [395 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [398 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [405 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [406 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [411 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [412 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [439 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [454 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [455 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [456 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [464 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [467 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [477 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [487 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [488 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [495 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [496 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [504 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [544 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [549 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [555 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [584 3 "// the program's own C faulted (cprog.go): the process a signal's end, as a C program's"] [607 1 "// reason writes why hsi stopped (HES43 (b)), a word beside its message, on a line of its own: \"hsi-reason: WORD\" (bin/hsi"] [608 1 "// check records it as the result's :reason, a class matches it by its :reasons)."] [611 1 "// fatalReason is the reason of a stop of hsi's own by its message: what it lacks (a primop, a Cmm primcall, a C function,"] [612 1 "// a function pointer, the RTS's API) or a state it cannot go on from (a deadlock), else fatal."] [631 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [658 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [672 6 "// a safe foreign call returning or the first delay expiring, whichever comes first"] [680 6 "// asleep in poll(2) until a descriptor is ready or the first delay expires (awaitEvent)"] [696 5 "// every thread waits for a safe foreign call (the threaded way): until one returns"] [703 4 "// the program's own C threads may still put into an MVar (hs_try_putmvar) or call in: they run first, and"] [704 4 "// while one lives no thread is deadlocked (GHC's: an MVar a C thread can reach by a stable pointer is alive)"] [731 1 "// cIdleNap is the longest nap of cIdle when none of the program's C threads can run now."] [734 1 "// cIdle lets the program's own C threads run while no Haskell thread can (queue 430; the C threads and the machine share"] [735 1 "// crt's baton, one runs at a time): the runnable ones first (crt's Yield), then, when no Haskell thread was woken, a nap of"] [736 1 "// at most d (cIdleNap) in crt's nanosleep, in which the C threads waiting for a time run as it comes. False when the C"] [737 1 "// started no thread or every one it started has ended."] [786 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [787 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [788 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [800 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [815 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [820 5 "// the allocation limit, checked every 256 bounces (GHC: at each nursery block, 4 KiB)"] [825 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [839 3 "// a case continuation run by ret may be compiled code that ran a yield# or a direct call to the budget's end"] [840 3 "// (HES74 (c): -O1's inline yield#, a forked thread's first chance): the slice ends here too, as it would"] [841 3 "// after the interpreter's eval of the alternative"] [852 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [857 3 "// exitScheduler (threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in foreign calls left"] [869 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [883 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [892 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [901 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [906 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [907 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [908 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [911 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [91